.TH MISTERDEV 1 "2026-07-11" "misterdev" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
misterdev \- autonomous LLM build orchestrator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B misterdev
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B misterdev
\(dq\fIplain-english request\fR\(dq
.br
.B misterdev
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B misterdev
points a large language model at a repository and a goal, reads the codebase as
a symbol graph, decomposes the goal into ordered tasks, edits code with anchored
SEARCH/REPLACE hunks, and runs every change through correctness gates (build,
lint, tests, typecheck) before reporting done. A change that regresses the test
suite is reverted through git; nothing merges unless it stays green.
.PP
There are three ways to drive it, from most guided to most explicit:
.TP
.B Interactive
Run
.B misterdev
with no arguments (or
.BR "misterdev i" )
for a guided menu \(em pick an action, answer a couple of prompts, confirm.
Nothing to memorize.
.TP
.B Natural language
If the first argument is not a known command, the whole line is treated as plain
English:
.B misterdev
maps it to an action with its own model, previews it, and asks before anything
mutating.
.TP
.B Flags
The subcommands and options below, for scripts and power users.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR interactive ", " i
Launch the guided interactive menu (also the no-argument default).
.TP
.B build \fR[\fIpath\fR] [\fIgoal\fR] [options]
Autonomously build, debug, or complete a goal in a project. The goal is free
text; the words \fBdebug\fR or \fBcomplete\fR select those modes.
.TP
.B run \fR[\fIpath\fR] [options]
Execute a project's pending tasks with dependency-aware ordering, parallel
waves, and progress-based resume.
.TP
.B plan \fR[\fIpath\fR] [options]
Analyze the project, recommend work, and compose a plan interactively.
.TP
.B status \fR[\fIpath\fR]
Show a project's tasks and their state.
.TP
.B report \fR[\fIpath\fR]
Summarize the latest build's cost, per-model ledger, and audit trail
(read-only).
.TP
.B scan \fIdir\fR
Discover and register projects (those with a \fBproject.yaml\fR) under a
directory.
.TP
.B list
List registered projects.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS build
.TP
.BI \-\-budget " DOLLARS"
Cap the run's spend (default 100).
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Plan only; show what would be done without editing.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-tasks " N"
Cap the number of decomposed tasks.
.TP
.B \-\-no-verify
Skip the final quality-gate chain.
.SS run
.TP
.BI \-\-tasks " FILE"
Execute an external task-list file instead of the \fBdevplan/\fR directory. The
file may live in another repository and be in any format \(em JSON, YAML,
Markdown, or plain text; ordered or unordered lists; multi-line tasks; phases;
and a dependency table (\fB| Task | Blocked By |\fR) that unlocks parallel
execution.
.TP
.BI \-\-task " ID"
Run a single task by id.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Show the execution plan (topological waves) without running.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Show which tasks would run vs. skip, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Re-run all tasks, ignoring the completion cache.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Guided menu (no flags):
.B misterdev
.TP
Plain English:
.B misterdev \(dqfix the flaky auth test but keep it cheap\(dq
.TP
Explicit build with a budget:
.B misterdev build . \(dqadd rate limiting to the public API\(dq \-\-budget 5
.TP
Run a hand-written task list from another repo, previewing first:
.B misterdev run ./app \-\-tasks ../plans/PLAN.md \-\-dry-run
.TP
Fix everything that is broken:
.B misterdev build . debug
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
Default API key variable (overridable via \fBllm.api_key_env_var\fR in
\fBproject.yaml\fR). The key is never written to config on disk.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B project.yaml
Per-project configuration (language, build/test/lint commands, gates, MCP,
targets, \fBtasklist\fR). See \fBdocs/configuration.md\fR.
.TP
.B devplan/
Directory of pre-written task files (Markdown + YAML front-matter).
.TP
.B .orchestrator/
Per-project run state: progress cache, contracts, worktrees, audit trail.
.TP
.B ~/.misterdev/registry.json
Registered-project cache. Stale entries (no \fBproject.yaml\fR) are pruned on
load.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation under \fBdocs/\fR: getting-started, configuration, mcp,
plugins. Homepage: https://github.com/dcondrey/misterdev
.SH AUTHOR
David Condrey.
